      "math_academy_id": "q-134849",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "A submarine navigates part of the deep sea. The submarine starts at a high position relative to the bottom of the sea and submerges until it reaches a deeper position. Later it returns near to its starting level. The submarine's distance to the bottom of the sea relative to time can be described using a quadratic curve. Which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?",
      "worked_solution": "For a quantity that varies quadratically, the points on the plot should be scattered along a parabola.\n\nAmong the given options, the only scatter plot that fits the description is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226611/assets/5b1d8d3c5e5661ca47cdba385b459491dffcb556cf38ab49cb092598763d057a.png)",
